  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string SSS that contains of the characters AAA, BBB or CCC only.\n\nIn one operation, you can do either of the following:\n\n\nChoose an occurrence of AB\\text{AB}AB in the string, convert it to BA\\text{BA}BA.\nChoose an occurrence of BC\\text{BC}BC in the string, convert it to CB\\text{CB}CB.\nNote that you are only allowed to operate on adjacent elements.\n\nFind the maximum number of operations you can do. It can be proven the answer is finite.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN - the length of the string.\nThe second line contains SSS - the string.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum number of operations possible.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "∣S∣=N|S| = N∣S∣=N",
      "Si∈{A,B,C}S_i \\in \\{A, B, C\\}Si​∈{A,B,C}",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n4\nABCC\n5\nBAABB\n2\nBA",
        "output": "2\n4\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : We can convert ABCC\\text{ABCC}ABCC to ACBC\\text{ACBC}ACBC and then to ACCB\\text{ACCB}ACCB. More than 222 operations can be proven to be impossible.\nTest Case 2 : BAABB→BABAB→BBAAB→BBABA→BBBAA\\text{BAABB} \\rightarrow \\text{BABAB} \\rightarrow \\text{BBAAB} \\rightarrow \\text{BBABA} \\rightarrow \\text{BBBAA}BAABB→BABAB→BBAAB→BBABA→BBBAA."
      }
    ]
  },
